.TH DIRENT64_NEXT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
dirent64_next \- decode one Linux directory record
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <dirent.h>
.PP
.BI "int dirent64_next(const char* " buffer ", long " byte_count ,
.BI "                  long* " position ", struct dirent64* " entry ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decode the next record in the bytes returned by
.BR getdents64 (3crunch).
Set
.I position
to zero for each new buffer. A successful call advances it by the record
length and fills the entry. The entry's
.B name
points into the input buffer and remains valid only until the buffer is
modified or released;
.B name_length
excludes the NUL terminator.
.B inode
and
.B offset
hold the kernel bit patterns in signed longs; offset is an opaque directory
position cookie, not an offset into the buffer.
.B kind
is a
.B DT_*
value and may be
.BR DT_UNKNOWN .
The function checks bounds and NUL termination, but the caller must provide
accessible storage and avoid changing the buffer while decoding it.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 for an entry or 0 at the end of the buffer, leaving
.B errno
unchanged. Returns \-1 with
.B errno
set to
.B EINVAL
for invalid arguments or malformed records; position and entry remain unchanged.
.SH NOTES
This interface decodes Linux x86\-64 records. Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getdents64 (3crunch),
.BR getdents64 (2)
